course: dictionary
lesson: 12624
title: Taking things apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dismantled is the past tense of dismantle. It has two main meanings. The first is to take something apart piece by piece. «Sam dismantled the tent so they could carry it home.» Sam did not throw the tent away. He took each pole and sheet apart.
explain: The second meaning is about ending or getting rid of something step by step, like a system, a law or an organisation. «The old rules were dismantled over ten years.» Nothing was smashed in one go. Each part was ended, one at a time.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. Ask yourself: is there a thing with parts? Then it means taken apart. Is there a system or a rule? Then it means ended step by step. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Dismantle means to take something apart piece by piece.
fact: «Dismantled» is the past tense of dismantle, so it tells you something already happened.
fact: «Dismantled» can also mean ended or got rid of step by step, like a system, a law or an organisation.
fact: In history, unfair systems such as apartheid were dismantled.
fact: The other forms of the word are dismantle, dismantles and dismantling.
exercise: «Sam dismantled the tent so they could carry it home.» What does dismantled mean here? | Put up in a hurry | *Taken apart piece by piece | Lost in the wind | Painted bright red
exercise: «The old rules were dismantled over ten years.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | Made louder and stronger | Copied onto a new page | *Ended step by step | Built up again from new materials
exercise: «The engineers dismantled the old machine before moving it.» Find and copy the word that means taken apart. | engineers | before | *dismantled | machine
test: «The students dismantled the bed frame to fit it through the door.» What does dismantled mean? | Painted in bright colours | *Taken apart piece by piece | Hidden under a sheet | Built up
test: «Over the years, the town dismantled its unfair system step by step.» What does dismantled mean here? | Forgotten about | *Ended or got rid of | Made stronger | Opened up to visitors
exam: Ama says, «The team dismantled the old rules, one by one.» Does dismantled mean taken apart or ended step by step? | Taken apart piece by piece | *Ended step by step | Painted over in white | Hidden in a box
